        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add Re-import Cookie button to OpenCode and OpenCode Go settings",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a ↻ trailing action button in the Cookie Source picker row for OpenCode Go and OpenCode providers in the settings pane.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n1. Clears the cached browser cookie from Keychain\n2. Re-imports from all supported browsers (using the provider's browser import order)\n3. Stores the fresh cookie\n4. Triggers an immediate provider refresh\n\nIf re-import fails (e.g. running outside the signed app bundle), the cache is still cleared and the next auto-refresh will complete the import.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe same code path (`CookieHeaderCache.clear` → `importSession` → `store`) is exercised by the CLI command. See `docs/proof/cli-cookie-refresh-proof.md` in PR #2262 for the full test matrix.\n\nButton UI verified via signed-app screenshot: located in the Cookie Source picker trailing area alongside the cached timestamp and source dropdown.\n\n## Related\n\n- Issue: https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/issues/2260\n- CLI PR: https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/pull/2262",
